 "comments": [
  {
   "address": 2721,
   "type": "line",
   "text": "\"LEVEL 001\" and \"GAME OVER\", screen codes + $80. A copy is at $CFA1; which one the code\nreads is not yet established."
  },
  {
   "address": 16640,
   "type": "line",
   "text": "The ten level cards, one per screen: out through forest, cinema, ghetto, graveyard and\nhaunted house, then back the other way. Each is row, column, PETSCII, $01. Each level's\nrecord at $7000 + $80 * n holds its card's address at +$74 ($5BDB reads it via zp $11)."
  },
  {
   "address": 22346,
   "type": "line",
   "text": "\"PRESS CTRL FOR MENU\", screen codes + $80. Copied to screen row 23 by show_press_ctrl;\nno JSR to that routine was found, so where it is used is open."
  },
  {
   "address": 23631,
   "type": "line",
   "text": "Show a card: print it, black border and background, multicolour text on, charset at $3000\n($D018 = $1C), then stamp \"MASTERTRONIC'S\" (screen codes + $80, 14 bytes) at $04D6, which is\nscreen row 5, column 14, in red."
  },
  {
   "address": 23768,
   "type": "line",
   "text": "Print a text card. X/Y = card address. Clears the screen (CHR$(147)), puts the cursor at\nthe card's first two bytes (row, column) through KERNAL PLOT, then prints PETSCII through\nCHROUT up to a $01 terminator. Colour and cursor control codes lay the card out."
  },
  {
   "address": 24778,
   "type": "line",
   "text": "Start the music: silence the SID, point the play position zp $B7/$B8 and the loop point\nzp $B9/$BA at the tune, set the filter and volume, and install music_irq in $0314."
  },
  {
   "address": 24821,
   "type": "line",
   "text": "The IRQ ($0314): count the step timer zp $02 down; at zero play the next command. Exits\nthrough the KERNAL's $EA31 via music_irq_exit."
  },
  {
   "address": 24843,
   "type": "line",
   "text": "Self-modified: music_next_command stores the command byte into $610C, so this JMP goes\nto $61xx, the handler for that byte."
  },
  {
   "address": 24956,
   "type": "line",
   "text": "Count: INC $02FF, which the game polls ($5DAD, $7614) to learn how far the tune has got."
  },
  {
   "address": 25042,
   "type": "line",
   "text": "Stop the music: silence the SID and give $0314 back to the KERNAL's $EA31."
  },
  {
   "address": 25065,
   "type": "line",
   "text": "Advance the play position and return the byte there in A."
  },
  {
   "address": 25080,
   "type": "line",
   "text": "The tune: command bytes, each the low byte of its handler's address in page $61, each\nfollowed by its operands (see music_dispatch). Played from $61F9 (music_fetch pre-increments)\nto the loop command $C7 at $6A15. Pitches are computed for the NTSC clock."
  },
  {
   "address": 30656,
   "type": "line",
   "text": "\"PROGRAMMED BY DAVID AND RICHARD DARLING.\", screen codes + $80, 40 bytes: one screen row."
  },
  {
   "address": 31744,
   "type": "line",
   "text": "The title card: welcome, the goal and the controls. Printed by $7760 after a game ends."
  }
 ]
}